From a5c0d8900253e5a549493ab4f7beb741c20c9ea4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:58:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): fence stored creator context during daily
 release [daveey]

Review 5991287623 found the ordinary-gate side of midnight release could borrow
its evaluating worker's admitted creator and exempt a detector-filed review.
Why: row_opts marked stored provenance, but only the daily-cap exemption read
that marker; the ordinary gate still resolved process env via _agent_task.
Fence at that shared resolver after explicit creator resolution, before either
env alias. Keep creation-context fallbacks unchanged. Auto-reset admissions
count daily cards without spending the independent planner admit budget.

Flow reports known failed required checks as ci, not unknown. Document the
strict first-nonempty-line COMMENT verdict contract; approval-like prose stays
unknown rather than guessed.

Proof: original seven new cases RED. Expanded midnight and raised-cap matrix
kills old fence on eight persisted cases (both cap kinds and env aliases).
Eleven consumer/docs files GREEN: 206 passed, 0 failed. Four exact-anchor
mutants killed; expanded baseline 65 passed and fence repeat kills all eight.
Full scripts/check: 21 checks ok. Read-only gate replay on hub boards and
sync-shadows: 35,303 rows in 20 DBs; 24 changed observations, 13 unique cards,
all done/archived, all inspected, no live-card change. Those creator-less rows
no longer borrow an evaluating worker's agent identity. No production caps
changed and no Desktop restart.
